RISC3D test kit 24 (prototype, 14 November 2026)
================================================

Your TORCS recording (ctx-477) draws correctly in software, both on the
build machine and on the Pi, and wrongly on the Pi's GPU. So RISC3D
passes TORCS's commands on correctly, and it's the GPU's driver that
draws something differently. This kit's rol-3d (0.13) redraws the
recording on the GPU with things left out, to find which.

Your ReplayGPU-240 shows exactly TORCS's fault (plain yellow car,
smeared scenery). 0.13 also reads every frame back during a replay, as
TORCS's frames were, so the GPU's work is split into frames as it was.

Steps
-----
 1. Copy RISC3DTest to HardDisc4 (unzip it there, replacing kit 23).
 2. In RiSH's Root shell:
      apt-get install /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/riscos-risc3d_0.13-1_arm64.deb
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/replay /riscos/3d/recorded/ctx-477.r3d 240
    It writes ReplayGPU-240, ReplayNoMip-240, ReplayNoHint-240 and
    ReplaySoft-240 (PPM pictures) into RISC3DTest.

